*  CN-7 -- CLEAR() MUST ACTUALLY CLEAR (found s149 while landing CN-6; FIXED s149).
*  Manual Ch.19 CLEAR: "If s is omitted, then the null string is assigned to all user
*  variables in the system."  ORACLE-MEASURED: both reads below come back null.
*  THE DEFECT (pre-existing, A/B-proven independent of CN-6): _CLEAR_ called
*  NV_CLEAR_fn, which stored NULVCL into NV_t.val UNCONDITIONALLY -- the one writer in
*  core.c that ignored the entry's GVA binding.  Every other site asks
*  `is_gva ? *cell : val` (2185/2227/2242/2302/2345), so CLEAR nulled a copy the
*  compiled program never reads and was SILENTLY A NO-OP for every ordinary variable.
*  The direct and the indirect read AGREE WITH EACH OTHER in both engines, which is the
*  point of pairing them: this was never an indirection defect and never a read-path
*  split -- it was CLEAR failing to reach the storage the program actually uses.
*  THE FIX stores through the binding the entry already carries and skips what is
*  protected (is_const per CN-6, and is_protected_pat_name per the manual's ARB rule).
*  Deliberately NOT routed through NV_SET_fn even though that is the store authority:
*  an I/O association sets g_call_fastpath_off, which would drag every entry through
*  _io_chan_find_by_var -- a bulk reset must not fire I/O associations.
        X = "gone"
        CLEAR()
        OUTPUT = "direct=[" X "]"
        OUTPUT = "indirect=[" $("X") "]"
END
